- `py_compile` of all three files passes; `validate_scenario_ids()` passes (9 IDs exactly once); corner/randomized classes confirmed to have no `SCENARIO_ID`.
- Padded blocks match the reference model for every length 0–55; all directed KAT digests equal `hashlib` and the plan's expected values.
- Import review: only public Cocotb 2.1.0 (`ClockCycles`, `FallingEdge`) and pyuvm 5.0.0 APIs (`uvm_sequencer`, `uvm_driver`, `uvm_sequence`, `ConfigDB`); no `ModifiableObject`, no `cocotb.handle`, no `int(dut.<pin>)`, no SystemVerilog.
- Confirmed the pyuvm item handshake (`start_item` → set fields → `finish_item` → driver `get_next_item` waits on `item_ready` → `item_done`) so field setting is race-free. No RTL simulator is installed here, so live simulation could not be run in this environment; a `__main__` sanity check is included in the sequences module.
