- `run_phase` is an `async def` synchronized on `RisingEdge(dut.clk)`, with 0→1 edge detection of `start` (one transaction per start pulse, width-independent). `block` is captured on the same sampling edge the RTL captures it on, per the driver's falling-edge settle convention (§11).
- Completion is **fixed-cycle only**: a per-start observer (`cocotb.start_soon` on the transaction) awaits `ClockCycles(clk, COMPLETION_MARGIN_CYCLES)` (70, §7), samples `done`/`digest`, sets `latency_cycles = 70`, and publishes exactly one `Sha256Transaction` (all six CONTRACT fields, monotonic in-order `txn_id`) via `ap.write(...)`. The broken `done` pin is never used as a completion indicator (DISC-001/013). Concurrent observers keep back-to-back / start-while-busy scenarios loss-free, and finish in start order for in-order scoreboard matching.
- X/Z samples are logged and mapped to 0 defensively (the documented `int(dut.<pin>.value)` read path is still used).

**`tb/sha256_agent.py`** — `Sha256Agent(uvm_agent)`: builds `sequencer`/`driver`/`monitor` children; `connect_phase` wires `driver.seq_item_port.connect(sequencer.seq_item_export)` (CONTRACT §11) and sets `self.ap = self.monitor.ap` — verified against pyuvm 5.0.0's broadcast-subscriber model, where a separate agent port would silently drop writes. Documented attributes for later stages: `agent.sequencer/driver/monitor/ap`.

